```

The header is in addition to — not instead of — the upstream notice. The full
MIT permission text for the adapted code is reproduced at the end of this
file. The per-file audit is recorded in
[`docs/compliance.md`](./docs/compliance.md).

## Code adapted from MIT projects

### yt-dual-subs (Dual Subtitles for YouTube)

- Source: <https://github.com/Gythiro/yt-dual-subs>
- Version used for reference: 3.7.0
- License: MIT
- Copyright: Copyright (c) 2026 Gythiro
- Used for:
  - `src/entrypoints/inject.ts` — MAIN-world capture of the player's own
    `/api/timedtext` request URL, the `fmt=json3` re-fetch, and the degraded
    acquisition paths.
  - `src/lib/transcript/bridge.ts`, `client.ts`, `parse.ts`, `url.ts` —
    validated `window.postMessage` bridge, SPA lifecycle, json3 parsing and
    track/URL selection.
  - `src/features/overlay/Overlay.tsx`, `OverlayView.tsx`, `position.ts`,
    `use-player-snapshot.ts` — bilingual overlay layout, control-bar lift,
    fullscreen/SPA handling and native-caption suppression lifecycle.
  - `src/lib/ui/page-style.ts` — the native-caption suppression rule
    (opacity, not `display:none`, so the caption DOM remains readable).
  - `src/lib/llm/client.ts`, `batch.ts` — BYOK, OpenAI-compatible translation
    channel shape and the retry/timeout policy.
- Not copied: the translation prompt text is Earworm's own; only the channel
  shape and retry policy were adapted.

### easysubs

- Source: <https://github.com/Nitrino/easysubs>
- Version used for reference: 3.1.3
- License: MIT
- Copyright: Copyright (c) 2022 Seo Jong Hak
- Used for:
  - `src/features/playback/attach.ts`, `controller.ts`, `keyboard.ts` —
    sentence-level previous / repeat / next seeking semantics, the YouTube
    `<video>` adapter lifecycle, and the typing-target keyboard guard.
- Earworm's key mapping (`a` / `s` / `d`) and the sentence-merging model are
  Earworm's own; only the navigation behaviour was adapted.

### SceneLingo

- Source: <https://github.com/umutgokbulak/SceneLingo>
- License: MIT
- Copyright: Copyright (c) 2026 Umut
- Used for: the playback pattern in `src/features/playback/controller.ts` and
  `keyboard.ts` — a requestAnimationFrame clock with a per-range latch for
  auto-pause, plus the keyboard-registration guards. The implementation is
  Earworm's; no SceneLingo file is vendored.
- Not copied: SceneLingo's word/phrase prompt text. Earworm writes its own
  translation and collocation prompt.
- Attribution is retained because the source was read and the playback
  pattern was adapted from it.

## Data

### ECDICT

- Source: <https://github.com/skywind3000/ECDICT>
- License: MIT (upstream `LICENSE`: Copyright (c) 2025 Linwei)
- Used for: `public/data/ecdict.json` (50,961 trimmed entries) and
  `public/data/lemmas.json` (surface form → lemma), generated by
  `pnpm build:ecdict` from `data/ecdict.csv` and `data/lemma.en.txt`. The
  large input files are not committed.
- Provenance caveat: the ECDICT repository is MIT-licensed, but its data is
  assembled from several upstream dictionaries and word lists whose
  individual terms are not itemised by ECDICT. Some third-party dictionary
  content may therefore carry additional attribution terms (including
  CC-BY-style terms). Earworm ships only a trimmed, derived word list and
  records this ambiguity here rather than claiming row-level provenance.
  Downstream redistributors should verify the upstream data provenance for
  their own use.

### OpenSubtitles collocations

- Source: <https://huggingface.co/datasets/vladvlasov256/opensubs-collocations>
- License: CC-BY 4.0
- Attribution: OpenSubtitles; Lison & Tiedemann 2016.
- Used for: `public/data/collocations.json` (9,289 cleaned bigrams), generated
  by `pnpm build:collocations` from `data/en.jsonl`. The input file is not
  committed. The generated file's `meta` repeats the source URL, license and
  attribution.
- Citation:

  > Pierre Lison and Jörg Tiedemann. 2016. *OpenSubtitles2016: Extracting
  > Large Parallel Corpora from Movie and TV Subtitles.* In Proceedings of the
  > Tenth International Conference on Language Resources and Evaluation
  > (LREC 2016), Portorož, Slovenia.

  This NOTICE is the attribution required by CC-BY 4.0 for that data.

